ize: 14px;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" style=\"font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><strong>How to use this list when reconciling</strong></p><ol class=\"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\" style=\"font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In the Bookkeeping module, open the client and work through your transactions as usual.<br><br></li><li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Post each transaction to one of the standard codes listed above, rather than a custom code (see the note on custom codes above).<br><br></li><li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Where a category has both an allowable and a disallowable version, choose the one that reflects how the cost is treated for tax. If you are unsure whether a cost is allowable, check the current HMRC guidance or with your accounting body.<br><br></li><li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Once your transactions are posted and reconciled, map and import the business into the MTD IT module. Figures are grouped into their MTD IT categories automatically, based on the codes you have used.<br><br></li><li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">On the summary screen, review the cumulative income and expense totals for the quarter and confirm they are complete and correct before you send your quarterly update.</li></ol><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" dir=\"ltr\"><br><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans